From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route 203's forest copies no lower past the third
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

East of Jubilife the forest is Route 203's strip by its south edge drawn
again every 2 tiles south (Port_RenderForestOnSouth), each an eighth of a
tile lower than the one before: the last were 2 tiles under the map south
of the scenery, Route 202's east forest, their trees standing in its first
row's. The first three copies step down as before; the rest stay as low
as the third.
---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 86bfc2f5..d514341b 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -6602,8 +6602,13 @@ static void Port_RenderSceneryPart(const LandDataManager *landDataMan, u8 index,
 
 // Over each such scenery map, the strip of the map north of it drawn
 // again 2, 4, ... tiles further south, the whole of the scenery map's
-// depth, each an eighth of a tile lower than the one before; each only while
-// its box is in the view.
+// depth, the first three each an eighth of a tile lower than the one
+// before, the rest as low as the third; each only while its box is in the
+// view. (Each lower again, the last were 2 tiles under the map south of
+// the scenery, Route 202's east forest: their trees stood in its first
+// row's (2026-11-08, from 186,806). Past the third they're far from
+// the route's ground; side by side, they only meet along an edge.)
+#define PORT_FOREST_ON_LOWEST 3
 static void Port_RenderForestOnSouth(const LandDataManager *landDataMan)
 {
     int width = landDataMan->mapMatrixWidth;
@@ -6630,7 +6635,7 @@ static void Port_RenderForestOnSouth(const LandDataManager *landDataMan)
             VecFx32 moved = position;
             GFXTestBox box;
 
-            moved.y -= k * (MAP_OBJECT_TILE_SIZE / 8);
+            moved.y -= (k < PORT_FOREST_ON_LOWEST ? k : PORT_FOREST_ON_LOWEST) * (MAP_OBJECT_TILE_SIZE / 8);
             moved.z += k * 2 * MAP_OBJECT_TILE_SIZE;
 
             // (the strip's box alone, moved: its columns, its trees' height)
